# Pairs with RetainedRestorable, at two passes. Without the activation-local
# prune guard an operator's PruneAsync and a scheduled cycle's prune run at
# once: one pass restores a depended-on row after the other has scanned and
# moved on, an increment then passes its check against the restored row, and
# the first pass deletes its base.
MODULE: RetainedRestorableConcurrentPasses
TARGET: RetainedRestorable
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: two retention passes run at once
PERTURBS: PruneList
BOUNDS: NumPasses = 2

--- FIND
    \* The activation-local guard, checked before the listing is read: a pass
    \* is skipped while another runs.
    /\ \A q \in Passes : prPh[q] = "idle"
--- REPLACE
    \* MUTATION: no prune guard.
    /\ TRUE
--- END